        "original_id": "8e09f10f-9f7f-52a7-a1b2-464da82bd8bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm, Liverpool Bay, Wales, Irish Sea, northeast Wales, Cheshire, Lancashire, Merseyside\n- Projects: offshore renewable power project\n- Ships: SS Ellan Vannin\n\nFacts:\n- North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm is Wales' first offshore wind farm.\n- North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm is the United Kingdom's first major offshore renewable power project.\n- Liverpool Bay is a bay of the Irish Sea.\n- Liverpool Bay lies between northeast Wales, Cheshire, Lancashire, and Merseyside on the eastern side of the Irish Sea.\n- SS Ellan Vannin served under the name \"Ellan Vannin\" for a further 26 years before being lost in a storm on 3 December 1909 in Liverpool Bay.",
